1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Halkjell Jonsson Huk=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Jon Halkjellson and Princess Margareta Haraldsdatter Gille 
2 CONT * Hallkjell Jonsson also Hallkjell Huk (1158 - April 3, 1194) was a feudal lord, Lendmann of Blindheim, Sunnmøre , [ 1 ] and one of the protagonists of the Norwegian Civil Wars . He was the son of Jon Hallkjellsson (b. 1125) and M
2 CONC argaret Haraldsdatter, daughter of Harald IV of Norway . [ 2 ] He supported the rebellion against Sverre of Norway , supporting the pretender Sigurd Magnusson , illegitimate son of Magnus V . He moved to the northern archipelagos 
2 CONC where he recruited the leader Olaf (brother-in-law ofHarald Maddadsson ) and the Øyskjegg , the last Viking warriors in Orkney and Shetland , a formidable fleet of which he became warlord and returned to establish his contingent a
2 CONC t Viken . Sverre had veterans Birkebeiner so the confrontation was assured and both forces found themselves in the battle of Florvåg with a high cost of lives, including Hallkjell's own.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Foster son of Halkjell, who was SIGURD Magnusson (-killed in battle Florevåg near Bergen 3 Apr 1194, bur Bergen Church of St Mary).  The Saga of King Sverre names "a boy named Sigurd a illegitimate son of King Magnus Erlingson" 
2 CONC as one of the conspirators with "Halkel son of Jon Hallkelsson"[519].  King of the Øyskjegger in Norway 1192.  The Saga of King Sverre records that "Sigurd Kingsson" was killed in battle "in the water at Floruvoe" and was buried i
2 CONC n "Marinkirk yard"[520]. . - http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORWAY.htm#MagnusKingNorwaydied1184A
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: '''RAGNHILD Erlingsdatter, daughter of ERLING Ormsen Skakke & his wife Kristin of Norway.''' Ragnhild & Halkjell married after 19 Jun 1179. Ragnhild was the widow of JON Thorbergsson. [https://heimskringla.no/wiki/Magnu
2 CONC s_Erlingsons_saga '''Erling had four illegitimate sons. One was called Reidar, another Øgmund - they each had their own mother. A third was called Finn and a fourth Sigurd,  their mother was Åsa den Lyse, and they were younger. Kr
2 CONC istin Kongedatter and Erling had a daughter, whose name was Ragnhild; she was married to Jon Torbergson from Randaberg. Kristin left the country with the man whose name was Grim Rusle; they went out to Miklagård, where they stayed
2 CONC  for a while, and they had a couple of children together.''']
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''RAGNVALD Hallkelsson ''' (1180 - 1217), was leader of the baglers , died assassinated in Haugsvik. (-murdered Husvik near Drøbak 1217, bur Oslo).  Stormann of the Bagler in Norway. - http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORWEGIAN%
2 CONC 20NOBILITY.htm#HallkelJonssondied1194
2 CONT * '''Agmund krökedans Hallkjellsson''' (1190 - 1264), lendmann - https://es.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hallkjell_Jonsson
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORWEGIAN%20NOBILITY.htm#HallkelJonssondied1194 Project MedLands, Norway Nobility]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''JON Halkelsson'''  married  ([1155])''' MARGARETA Haraldsdatter,''' illegitimate daughter of HARALD "Gille" King of Norway & his mistress ---.  Snorre names "Harald Gille's third daughter…Margaret who was married to Jon Halke
2 CONC lson, a brother of Simon"[233].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jon & his wife MARGARETA Haraldsdatter had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * (a)      ''' HALLKEL Jonsson''' (-killed in battle Florevåg near Bergen 3 Apr 1194).  From Blindheim Jarl in Norway.  married (after 19 Jun 1179) as her second husband, '''RAGNHILD Erlingsdatter, widow of JON Thorbergsson,''' da
2 CONC ughter of ERLING Ormsen Skakke & his wife Kristin of Norway .  The Saga of King Sverre records the marriage of "Ragnhild daughter of Earl Erling and Kristin Kings-daughter" and "Halkel son of Jon Hallkelsson"[234].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Hallkel & his wife RAGNHILD Erlingsdatter had one child:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * (1)       '''RAGNVALD Hallkelsson''' (-murdered Husvik near Drøbak 1217, bur Oslo).  Stormann of the Bagler in Norway. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Biography=
2 CONT
2 CONT Liegeman. Parents: Jon Hallkjellsson and Margret Haraldsdotter. Married with Ragnhild Erlingsdotter, child of Erling Ormsson Skakke (died 1179) and Kristin Sigurdsdotter. Aunt of King Harald Gille.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hallkjell Jonsson was of lendman from Blindheim in western Norway and was a key player in mutual strife of 1180 to 1190, mostly as an opponent of King Sverre. In Sverre saga, which are main the source of Hallkjell's life, we find 
2 CONC Hallkjell and occasionally Magnus Erlingsson. But the saga unfortunately does not show a complete image, and it is difficult to find evidence that his loyalty was anchored in one or the other camp.
2 CONT
2 CONT He moved to the archipelagos in the north where he recruited the leader Olaf (brother of Harald Maddadsson ) and Øyskjegg , the last Viking warriors in Orkney and Shetland, a formidable fleet which became military chief and set ba
2 CONC ck its contingent in Viken . Sverre had veterans birkebeiner so the confrontation was secured and both forces met at the Battle of Florvåg with a high cost in lives among which joined the Hallkjell.
2 CONT
2 CONT After a short residence in Denmark Hallkjell returned to Norway together with Magnus 1184. It was also probably also at this time Hallkjell lasted married Ragnhild, daughter of Erling Skakke. The prince her husband, Jon of Randabe
2 CONC rg, died 1179, Erling, the marriage with Hallkjell came into being before King Magnus' fall 1184. Ragnhild had lost her father, her brother and her husband in the fight against Sverre Sigurdsson, and we can, realizing that there w
2 CONC as not completely unproblematic that her new husband. For Hallkjell that was hardly the case and was less complicated. Well, he was the brother-in-law to Magnus and son-in-law to Erling Skakke, but he was also the cousin of Sverre
2 CONC . 1192 we meet Hallkjell again, this time serving as King Sverre's liegeman.
2 CONT
2 CONT We can only speculate that it was Ragnhild who Hallkjell forced his servitude to King Sverre (Munch 1852), or whether the work placement with Sverre proximity must be considered acting as a "ufriviljugt intermezzo (Bull de 1931)".
2 CONC  The Sverre saga did note that Hallkjell advised together with Olaf Svogeren Haraldsson Earl of Orkney. The plan was to stage a rebellion against King Sverre. The revolt then names for the soldiers from the west of the sea, from t
2 CONC he Orkneys.
2 CONT
2 CONT Halkel and Ragnhild had previously fostered an illegitimate child of Magnus Erlingsson. It has been speculated that Sigurd did not know of this child (Stølen 1988 Koht 1958). Mora Gyrid, daughter of Aslak the Young. This Aslak ref
2 CONC ferd to Halkel Jonsson as uncle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Early review on sommaren 1193 came Halkel and Olav to Norway with 23 ships, but the crucial assaults against BIRKEBEINER did not come until the following year, with the battle in Florvåg at Bergen. In this battle fall Halkel, toge
2 CONC ther with future king and the bulk of øyskjeggflokken.
2 CONT
