1 SUBM @S6000000011260019676@
1 OBJE
2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p13/43/a3/d6/6f/5344485fff71f996/guttorm_eriksson_original.jpg?hash=f772dcab3ef085f4c1965cedfc398f2cd4a53a1bb955e64a49aa18777f2791da.1797667199
2 FORM jpg
2 _PRIM Y
1 OBJE
2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p13/a4/e9/06/a7/5344484168f94d57/gutthormi_filii_erici_original.jpg?hash=771df1736c5ba6d5892b96ff7372af3cedc5b53c99b6856d987ef1fc70fed2d5.1797667199
2 FORM jpg
2 NOTE Drawing of 13/14th century signet found in Sørum October 2016 by metal detectorist Stefan Tariczky. Submitted for curation to the county archeologist. Gutthormi Filii Erici (Gutthorm Eriksson) descended from the Sudrheim family on
3 CONC  his mothers side (rose surrounded by cuspate border) and possibly the Skior family on his fathers side (birds wing). The depicted seal may (or may not) have belonged to Guttorm Eirksson the brother of Paal Eirksson Skior. It may 
3 CONC also have belonged to Guttorm Eiriksson Hudfat who used the Sudrheim CoA. Both Guttorm Eiriksson (Skior) and Guttorm Eirksson Hudfat are mentioned as sysselmann in Southern Gudbrandsdal in the same time period. The depicted seal b
3 CONC egs the question weather these two Guttorm Eiriksson´s may have been the same person.
