1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''BIOGRAPHY'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Gunleik Viljalmson was Marshal (''staller'', ''stallare''), one of the Great Officers of State. According to Heber (1944: 153), Gunleik was 'likely' a son of William III of Torgar, but Heber does not provide arguments or evidence 
2 CONC for this claim. It should be observed that Gunleik Viljalmson may not have been identical with Gunleik Sneis, to whom the patronymic Viljalmson often has been attributed.
