2 CONT • # 1 Posted March 1, 2011 Sira Andres Ogmundsson f. About 1315, died after 1395, was a clergyman at Hamar and parish priest at Hoff, Toten, mentioned in various letters from 1341 to 1393. He was probably father of Magnild Andresd
2 CONC atter who was married to Torstein Skjeldulvsson from Månsta in Jemtland.   But who was father of Andres? In some places, Ogmund Guttormsson of Bolt family is listed. But I have seen a family record where there is an Ogmund Saxesso
2 CONC n, son of Saxe Ivarsson, who is again set up as a brother of baron Jon Ivarsson Raud from Sudreim. But has this Saxe Ivarsson existed? I have not seen referring to him anywhere else.   Are there any of you medieval connoisseurs wh
2 CONC o know something about this?
2 CONT
2 CONT • # 2 Posted March 8, 2011 I take the chance to retrieve this one again, hoping somebody bites. <BR> <BR> I know that Ogmund Saxesson was a lawyer on the 13th century Oppland, living at Sakslund in Stange, but that he should be a 
2 CONC son By a Saxe Ivarsson, is probably only a construction. Or? <BR> <BR> Nonetheless, I can not find any credible sources that say anything about who was Andres Ogmundsson's father.
2 CONT
2 CONT • # 3 Posted March 8, 2011 It might be interesting to know what you have on the basis of the different things here. I'm here with a copy of N. Stene's article "Tom on Råde" from NST VII. Here is a possible relationship between Mr.
2 CONC  Ogmund Guttormsson on Tom and Sira Andres Ogmundsson. He runs a series of indications, but finally concludes: "But although it fits both the weapon, the father's name and the time, I do not dare to put up Sir Andres as son of Mr.
2 CONC  Obmund Guttormsson on Tom (...)".   Nor is Mr. Ogmund a Bolt to confirm. It is indisputable in name and landlord, but he led himself to another weapon than Boltane. That Sira Andres was the father of Magnhild married Thorstein Sk
2 CONC jeldulvsson, however, hosted the confirmation of Stene. If there is enough newer literature on the subject, I do not know about diverging.
2 CONT
2 CONT • # 4 Posted March 8, 2011 By the way: A little "googling" shows that on the net there are unpublished links to the Bolts where Mr Ogmund Guttormsson is to marry Sigrid, daughter of Knight and Riksråd, Håkon Ogmundsson [bolt]. I a
2 CONC m also here with the duplicates of Henning Sollied's articles on "Sourcecritical Studies on Some Middle Age Leads" about the Bolts in NST VII, where he concludes: 1. Mr. Håkon has had a daughter Sigrid 2. Mrs Sigrid is married to 
2 CONC one Ogmund and has one famous son, Oluf Ogmundsson 3. This Ogmund and the son Oluf are not otherwise known If no more recent literature has been published, this will not be possible to confirm.
2 CONT
2 CONT • # 5 Posted March 8, 2011 Håvard - Thank you for your reply. I have, among other things, Read Per Reidar Christiansen's article "The old descendants of Månstad in Nes on Jemtland" in NST 38 2002, as well as Lars Løberg's "Torstei
2 CONC n Skjeldulvsson and his closest family" in NST 39 2003 and Christiansens correspond to the same number. Besides, I've been through Roger de Robelin's "Skanke ætten" and Stange village book by Svein-Erik Ødegaard. I have also seen 
2 CONC Stenes "Tom in Råde", as you refer to. "But I have seen the information about the connection with this Saxe Ivarsson in a family list on the Internet, which I unfortunately did not list the address.
2 CONT
2 CONT • # 6 Posted March 8, 2011 I would like to have one or another city here, NST article ... Get out of here. Does Roblin ever know about Stene / Sollied?
2 CONT
2 CONT '''• # 7 Posted March 8, 2011 The Robelin states that Magnild Andresdotter's parents were Anders (Andres) Guttormsson and Sigrid Håkansdotter (Bolt). This is, as you say, not documented and also referred to in the articles I refer
2 CONC  to.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''Sigrid Håkonsdatter Bolt''', 1
2 CONT
2 CONT Same as
2 CONT * https://www.geni.com/people/Sigrid-Haakonsdatter/6000000018985306207
2 CONT
2 CONT Helsyster till Borghild Haakonsdatter Bolt, Borghild, namngiven efter sin farmor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigrid, troligen namngiven efter sin moder eller mormor, halvsyster till Sigrid född i  faderns andra äktenskap, även hon döpt efter första hustrun eller dennes mormor, gift med Ogmund Guttormson Råde, alternativt en Ogmund N.N..
2 CONT
2 CONT I vilket fall som helst, då det här handlar om LOGIK i brist på bättre källhänvisningar ger det att om Sigrid verkligen var dotter till Håkon Bolt, så lär hon knappast ha haft två makar samtidigt, inte ens en skilsmässa från den e
2 CONC na löser problemet att bägge makarna är samtida och knappast kan ha varit gifta med en och samma kvinna SAMTIDIGT:
2 CONT
2 CONT Om nu Sigrid endast varit gift med en Ogmund N.N. som dött före ca.1300, så hade problemet med maken Hallstein varit ur vägen, men "Flera forskare hävdar att denne Sigrid Håkonsdotter är identisk med Sigrid Håkonsdotter Bolt , som
2 CONC  också var gift med Ogmund (Hirdt Jore) Guttormsson, riddare och hirdstjore, nämnd 1339- 1354 i Norge." vilket ger oss bara en logisk utväg, det fanns två stycken Sigrid och de var sannolikt halvsyskon, därmed får vi att endast en
2 CONC  av dem varit gift med Ogmund Guttormsen, medan den andre var gift med Hallstein.
2 CONT
2 CONT Det hör även till gammal tradition att namnge barn efter sin första hälfts bortgång, den andre frun får en dotter som döpts efter första avlidna frun, även döttrar vars mor dött i barnsäng ärades ofta med sin moders namn, i det hä
2 CONC r fallet är det troligt att den första hustrun dött i barnsäng vilket gett upphov till senare problem att få ihop Sigrids makar, men ingen kvinna mig veterligt, skulle kunnat ha haft två makar samtidigt under medeltiden och därmed
2 CONC  kan inte Ogmund N.N. vara identisk med  Ogmund Guttormsson, allt detta förutsatt att de såkallade experterna i ämnet har rätt förstås, vilket med denna lösning ger dem alla rätt.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigrid var dotter av riksrådet och sysslomanen i Ringerike, herr Håkon Ogmundsson [Bolt-vapen ,NS: 452)
2 CONT * Källa: Norska Sigiller av Huitfeldt och Kaas sid 452
