1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} <br/>
2 CONT Of his children Hallvard inherited the Roaldstad Farm and Tone the Lindheim Nordre Farm. In local  history books and on the Internet, we find various allegations that he was the Torbjørn Hallvardsson  or Halvorsson married to Lady
2 CONC  Elin to Asdal. She was either Eiliv Brynjulvsson to Asdal’s daughter or an  illegitimate daughter of Henrik Jensson Gyldenløve to Austrått, the father-in-law to Inger Ottesdatter  Rømer, Henrik Ibsen’s “Lady Inger to Ostrat”. Thi
2 CONC s is based on a false testimony in the legal processes  about the Asdal Estate in the sixteenth and seventeenth century. The first alternative is correct. However, she had no connection to this family. If so, members of this fami
2 CONC ly too had been involved in the  Asdal Case, which they were not.<br/>
2 CONT <br/><br/>
2 CONT <br/><br/>
2 CONT Drangedal & Tørdal p. 690, Sauherad III p. 870 and Sauherad IV p. 102<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
