2 CONT Se: Rog. Historie- og Ættesogelag: Ætt og Heim 1995 side 9 
2 CONT
2 CONT AI: 
2 CONT Sigurd Brynjulfson Aga was a notable Norwegian knight and lawman from the late 13th century. He was a representative of the emerging Norwegian aristocracy, influenced by broader European cultural and societal developments1. Sigurd
2 CONC  served as a knight, royal councilor, and lawman, and he is known for his association with the royal court, although he wasn’t among the top advisors1.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigurd lived at Aga in Ullensvang, Hardanger, where the “Lagmannsstova” (Lawman’s House) is preserved1. His coat of arms featured a beam between three lilies, a symbol that later became part of the municipal coat of arms for Ullen
2 CONC svang2.
