2 CONT
2 CONT When Jon Tallaksson's father died in 1522, he inherited the entire
2 CONT
2 CONT Aukland farm, which was valued at 2 1/2 laupar butter. He is named in
2 CONT
2 CONT the tax lists of 1519 and 1521. In 1521, Jon had to pay 22 marks 3
2 CONT
2 CONT shillings, as well as 26 lodd silver and 4 marks 2 shillings in tax.
2 CONT
2 CONT This shows that he was a very rich man. Jon is also named in the
2 CONT
2 CONT probate document of 1522 detailing the division of his father's
2 CONT
2 CONT estate. That document still exists and is preserved at the Aukland
2 CONT
2 CONT farm. He is last named in 1565 and probably died shortly thereafter.
2 CONT
