2 CONT James first married, in 1221, Eleanor, daughter of Alfonso VIII of Castile and Leonora of England. Though he later had the marriage annulled, his one son by her was declared legitimate:
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. Alfonso (1229–1260), married Constance of Montcada, Countess of Bigorre
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1235, James remarried to Yolanda, daughter of Andrew II of Hungary by his second wife Yolande de Courtenay. She bore him numerous children:
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. Yolanda, also known as Violant, (1236–1301), married Alfonso X of Castile
2 CONT    2. Constance (1239–1269), married Juan Manuel, Lord of Villena, son of Ferdinand III
2 CONT    3. Peter (1240–1285), successor in Aragon, Catalonia, and Valencia
2 CONT    4. James (1243–1311), successor in Balearics and Languedoc
2 CONT    5. Ferdinand (1245–1250)
2 CONT    6. Sancha (1246–1251)
2 CONT    7. Isabella (1247–1271), married Philip III of France
