2 CONT Succeeded 1331, died 1358 Married Isabella de Strathern, daughter of Malise, Earl of Caithness, Strathern, and Orkney.  Malise had no male heirs and after William’s death, his and Isabella’s son Henry was recognised as 42nd Earl o
2 CONC f Orkney in 1369 and ten years later as the first St Clair Prince of Orkney. In addition to the titles inherited from his father, Henry also became Lord Shetland, Lord Sinclair, Lord Chief Justice of Scotland, Admiral of the Seas,
2 CONC  Great Protector, and Keeper and Defender of the Prince of Scotland.
