2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#MaliseStrathearndied1271B
2 CONT
2 CONT MALISE, son of ROBERT Earl of Strathearn & his wife --- (-[in France] [before 23 Nov] 1271, bur Dunblane).  He succeeded his father in 1244 as Earl of Strathearn. He was one of the Regents of Scotland from 14 Sep 1255 to 1262. Mar
2 CONC ried firstly (1244 or before) to MARJORY de Muschamp, daughter of ROBERT de Muschamp of Wooler & his wife Isabel --- ([1226]-[12 Oct 1251/20 Mar 1255]). Married secondly (before 12 Dec 1257) to MAUD of Caithness, daughter of GILBE
2 CONC RT Earl of Caithness and Orkney. Married thirdly ([1261/62] or before) to EMMA, daughter of ---.  Married fourthly ([1268]), as her second husband, to MARY of Argyll, widow of MAGNUS King of Man, daughter of EWEN of Argyll & his w
2 CONC ife --- (-[28 Sep 1300/10 Oct 1303], buried in London, Grey Friars Church).  
2 CONT The Liber Pluscardensis records the marriage of "regulus Manniæ…viduam…filiam domini de Arcadia" and "comes de Strathern Malisius" [156].  The primary source which confirms her name has not yet been identified.   She married third
2 CONC ly (before 5 Apr 1281) Sir Hugh Abernethy of that Ilk, and fourthly (before 10 Apr 1299) as his second wife, William FitzWarin.  Earl Malise & his first wife had one child: 1.         MURIEL ([1244]-[16 May/12 Nov] 1291).  m (afte
2 CONC r 1267) as his second wife, WILLIAM Earl of Mar, son of DUNCAN Earl of Mar & his wife --- (-1281 before 25 Jul).  Earl Malise & his second wife had one child: 2.         
2 CONT
2 CONT MALISE ([1257]-[28 Jan/25 Mar] 1313, buried in Inchaffray Abbey). He succeeded his father in 1271 as Earl of Strathearn.  He swore fealty to Edward I King of England at Stirling 12 Jul 1291, and did homage to King Edward in 1296. 
2 CONC He was imprisoned in Rochester Castle in Nov 1306 for his alleged submission to Robert Bruce, but freed in Dec 1308 provided he lived in England.  
2 CONT He is said to have been captured by his son, who fought for the Scots, at Perth 28 Jan 1313. Married (1275 or before) AGNES Comyn, daughter of ALEXANDER Comyn Earl of Buchan & his wife Elizabeth de Quincy of Winchester (-after [28
2 CONC  Jan/25 Mar] 1313). Malise & his wife had two children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         MALISE ([1275/80]-before 1329). He succeeded his father in 1313 as Earl of Strathearn. Married firstly AGNES --- (-after 1311). Married secondly ([1323]), as her first husband,JOAN Menteith, daughter of Sir JOHN Menteit
2 CONC h of Rusky & his wife --- (-after 20 Mar 1367). She married secondly John Campbell Earl of Atholl, thirdly Maurice Moray Earl of Strathearn, and fourthly (before 9 Nov 1347) as his second wife, William Sutherland 5th Earl of Suthe
2 CONC rland.
2 CONT  Earl Malise & his first wife had two children: 
2 CONT i)          MALISE (-killed in battle Neville´s Cross 17 Oct 1346). He succeeded his father as Earl of Strathearn. He succeeded his cousin Magnus as Earl of Caithness and Orkney in [1323/29]. He resigned the earldom of Strathearn 
2 CONC [24 Sep/16 Dec] 1332 into the hands of Edward Balliol, was tried for treason in 1344 for so doing, but found innocent [157]. The Chronicle of John of Fordun (Continuator - Annals) records that "the Earl of Stratherne" was killed i
2 CONC n battle "at Durham" 17 Oct 1346 [158].  [159] Married firstly MARY, daughter of ---.  Married secondly ([1325/28]) MAUD [Marjory] of Ross, daughter of HUGH Earl of Ross & his first wife Maud Bruce (-after 1350). 
2 CONT ...
2 CONT Earl Malise & his first wife had four children: 
2 CONT (a)       MAUD . Married --- de la Arde .  
2 CONT (b)       EUPHEME .  
2 CONT (c)       AGNES . Married ERNGILS ---.  He was granted the title of Earl of Orkney by the king of Norway in right of his wife but forfeited it in 1375 [160].  
2 CONT (d)       ISABEL . Married Sir WILLIAM St Clair. 
2 CONT  ii)        MARY .  [161] Married ([1319/22]) as his second wife, Sir JOHN Moray of Drumsagard, co. Lanark, son of ---.  
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         MAUD (-before 1348).  m (1293) ROBERT de Tosny Lord Tosny (1276-1309).  
2 CONT
