2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/tree/4253637/person/25344128696/media/9?pgnum=1&pg=32914&pgpl=pid%7cpgNum Notes V. William Sinclair of Roslin was a minor when his father died, and succeeded to the pensions of his father and his Uncle Jo
2 CONC hn.  He had a Charter from King David II of the lands of Morton and Merchamyston in Midlothian, on the resignation of William Bisset on February 10, 1357/58. He had a safe conduct to go to England on May 6, 1358 on his way abroad 
2 CONC to Prussia to fight in foreign wars.  On September 17, 1358 King David II confirmed to him  an annuity granted to his grandfather Sir Henry S. Clair.      William married Isabella, second daughter of Malise, 8th Earl of Strathearn
2 CONC , Earl of Orkney and Caithness and his wife Marjorie, a daughter of Hugh, 4th Earl of Ross and Lady Maud Bruce, a sister of Scotland's national hero, King Robert the Bruce. Marjorie was a sister of William, 5th Earl of Ross. Willi
2 CONC am Sinclair left issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT •	Henry, shown next. •	David, who had a charter under the Great Seal of the lands of Newburgh and Auchdale in Aberdeenshire in exchange for any rights which he had in Orkney and Shetland, derived from his mother, dated April 23, 1
2 CONC 391.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/tree/4253637/person/25344128696/media/8?pgnum=1&pg=32914&pgpl=pid%7cpgNum
