2 CONC n to return to him, but she refused.  Their reciprocal complaints were once more brought up, but this time Gudrun had lensmann Erik Byre testify that he had seen her bleeding after an assault by her husband. Olav answered that Gud
2 CONC run had inflicted the damage herself and even given him a black eye, which the parish priest could confirm.  Again the court ordered a separation, but this time for two more years. Here the story ends and there is no record that t
2 CONC he fueding couple ever reconciled. Gudrun's estate was probated on 23 April 1617, but some of her heirs were dissatisfied with the outcome and another probate had to be held on 9 December 1621 to settle the estate.
