2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* a)         '''INGE Baardsson''' (-23 Apr 1217).  Morkinskinna names “Guthormr at Rein” as father of “Bárdr, the father of King Ingi and Skúli jarl”[244].  Snorre names "Guthorm of Reine" as grandfather of "King Inge and Duke
2 CONC  Skule", their father presumably being Baard although this is not stated in this passage[245].  King of the Birkebeiner.  He succeeded as King of Norway in 1204.  The Icelandic Annals record the death in 1204 of "rex Haquinus, Sve
2 CONC rreri filius" and the succession of "Ingo Bardi filius" aged 13 [although this age appears inconsistent with the chronology of the family][246].  
