1 OCCU Prinsessa, Princess of Sweden
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Ingeborg Eriksdotter''', född någon gång mellan sina föräldrars giftermål 1210 och sin fars död 1216. Död 17 juni 1254, var en svensk prinsessa, dotter till kung Erik Knutsson och drottning Rikissa, gift med jar
2 CONC len Birger Magnusson och stammoder för kungaätten Bjälboätten.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Project MedLands Sweden Kings==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''BIRGER Magnusson, son of MAGNUS "Minnesköld" [Folkungaätten] & his second wife Ingrid [Ylva] ''''([1200]-20/21 Oct 1266, bur Varnhem Abbey).  The Icelandic Annals record that "dominus Birgerus Magni filius" was made "comes in S
2 CONC vecia" in 1248[173].  Jarl at Bjälbo.  Regent of Sweden.  Founder of Stockholm.  “B…Dux Sueorum” donated property to Eskilstuna Kloster by charter dated 16 Jul 1266 which names “filiorum nostrorum…W…Regis Sueorum, Magni Ducis…Eric
2 CONC j ac Benedictj Scolaris”[174].  The Icelandic Annals record the death in 1265 of "Birgerus dux Sveciæ"[175]. 
2 CONT '''m firstly ([1235]) INGEBORG of Sweden, daughter of ERIK Knutsson King of Sweden & his second wife Richeza of Denmark ([1212]-17 Jun 1254). ''' Her marriage is confirmed by a charter dated 4 Nov 1246 in which “Ericus…rex Swethie
2 CONC ” names “domino Birgero genero nostro”[176].  The primary source which confirms her name has not yet been identified.  m secondly (1261) as her second husband, MECHTILD von Holstein, widow of ABEL King of Denmark, daughter of ADOL
2 CONC F IV Graf von Holstein und Stormarn & his wife Hedwig zur Lippe (1225-1288, bur Varnhem Abbey).  The Annales Stadenses record the marriage "1237 VII Kal Mai" of "dux Abel" and "filiam comitis Adolfi de Scowenborch", naming her "Me
2 CONC chtildem" and recording her second marriage to "ducem Sueciæ" in a later passage[177].  The Icelandic Annals record the marriage in 1261 of "Bergerus Sveciæ dux" and "Mathildam reginam Daniæ"[178].  Mistress (1): ---.  The name of
2 CONC  Birger's mistress is not known. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Birger Magnusson & his first wife INGEBORG had eight children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.         '''RIKISSA  Birgersdotter ''' (-before 13 Dec 1288).  The Cronica Principum Saxonie names "Rixam filiam regis Suecie" as wife of "Henricum seniorem [filium Nycolai domini de Werle]"[179].  The primary source which con
2 CONC firms her first marriage has not yet been identified.  m firstly (Oslo 1251) HAAKON Haakonsson "den Unge/the Young" under King of Norway, son of HAAKON IV "den Gamle/the Old" King of Norway & his wife Margareta Skulesdotter (Berge
2 CONC n 10 Nov 1232-Tønsberg 30 Apr or 5 May1257, bur Oslo, St Hallvards Church).  m secondly (1262) as his first wife, HEINRICH von Werle, son of NIKOLAUS I Herr von Werle zu Rostock [Mecklenburg] & his wife Jutta von Anhalt (-murdered
2 CONC  near Saal, Rügen 8 Oct 1291).  Herr zu Werle zu Güstrow 1281. 
2 CONT * 2.         '''VALDEMAR Birgersson''' ([1237]-Nyköping Castle 26 Dec 1302).  The Icelandic Annals record that "Valdemarus Birgiri filius" succeeded as king of Sweden in 1249[180].  He succeeded in 1250 as VALDEMAR King of Sweden.
2 CONC   “Waldemarus…rex Swechie” confirmed the donation of property to Gudhems Kloster by “reginam dominam Katerinam” by charter dated 17 Jan 1251 which names “patris nostri domini Byrgerj ducis”[181].  The Annales Lubicenses records th
2 CONC at "Waldemarus rex Sweorum" was deposed in 1275 by "Magno duce fratre suo"[182].  The Icelandic Annals record the reconcilation between "reges Valdemarus et Magnus" and the departure of Valdemar for Denmark soon after[183].  The I
2 CONC celandic Annals record the death in 1302 of "Valdemarus Birgeri filius Rex Sveonum"[184].  m firstly (1260, divorced after 1276) SOPHIE of Denmark, daughter of ERIK IV "Plovpenning" King of Denmark & his wife Jutta of Saxony (-128
2 CONC 6).  The Icelandic Annals record a visit to "Konúngahellam…festo martyris Albani" by "rex Valdemarus Sophiaque regina cum filio domicello Erico annos quinque nato" in 1276[185].  The Icelandic Annals note the presence of "Sophia r
2 CONC egina Valdimari regis, eorumque filio Erico domicello et filiabus Ingeburga quæ nupsit Gerhardo filio Gerhardi comitis Holsatiæ et Catharina virgine" at the reconcilation between "reges Valdemarus et Magnus"[186].  m secondly LUCA
2 CONC RDIS, daughter of ---.  1296.  The primary source which confirms her marriage has not yet been identified.   Mistress (1): JUTTA of Denmark, daughter of ERIK IV "Plovpenning" King of Denmark & his wife Jutta of Saxony ([1246]-[128
2 CONC 6/95]).  Abbess of St Agneta in Roskilde 1266.  She left the convent in 1271[187].  King Valdemar had & his first wife had seven children: 
2 CONT >>>>* a)         ERIK Valdemarsson (-1261, bur Sigruna Abbey).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  
2 CONT >>>>* b)         INGEBORG Valdemarsdotter (-[1290]).  The Annales Lubicenses refer to the first wife of "Gherardi comitis Holtzatiæ" as "filia Woldemari Regis Sweciæ"[188].  “Waldemarus…Rex Sveorum” confirmed a grant to Hamburg by
2 CONC  “pater noster Dominus Byrgerus felicis memoriæ Dux Sveorum” by charter dated 12 Dec 1275 “in nuptiis filiæ nostræ…et comitis Gerardi…de Holsatia”[189].  The Icelandic Annals note the presence of "Sophia regina Valdimari regis, eo
2 CONC rumque filio Erico domicello et filiabus Ingeburga quæ nupsit Gerhardo filio Gerhardi comitis Holsatiæ et Catharina virgine" at the reconcilation between "reges Valdemarus et Magnus"[190].  m (12 Dec 1275) as his first wife, GERHA
2 CONC RD II Graf von Holstein in Plön, son of GERHARD I Graf von Holstein in Itzehoe & his first wife Elisabeth von Mecklenburg (1254-Plön 28 Oct 1312, bur Hamburg Cathedral).
2 CONT >>>>* c)         KATARINA Valdemarsdotter (-1283).  The Icelandic Annals record a visit to "Konúngahellam…festo martyris Albani" by "rex Valdemarus Sophiaque regina cum filio domicello Erico annos quinque nato" in 1276[191]. 
2 CONT >>>>* d)         ERIK Valdemarsson [Folkungaättens Valdemarsgren] ([1271/72]-1330).  The Icelandic Annals record a visit to "Konúngahellam…festo martyris Albani" by "rex Valdemarus Sophiaque regina cum filio domicello Erico annos 
2 CONC quinque nato" in 1276[192].  The Icelandic Annals record a visit to "Konúngahellam…festo martyris Albani" by "rex Valdemarus Sophiaque regina cum filio domicello Erico annos quinque nato" in 1276[193].  The Icelandic Annals record
2 CONC  that "domicellus Ericus filius Valdemari" was released from prison in 1302[194].  Norwegian High Councillor 1308.  Swedish High Councillor 1322.  m INGEBORG Knutsdotter, daughter of KNUT Jonsson [Aspenäsätten] & his wife Katharin
2 CONC a Bengtsdotter [Folkungaättens lagmansgren].  1333.  Erik & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT >>>>>>* i)          VALDEMAR Eriksson .  1345/69.  m firstly (before 1347) INGEGÄRD Karlsdotter [Färla], daughter of [KARL Orestason [Färla] & his wife Helena Magnusdotter [Folkungaättens oäkta gren]].  m secondly as her first hus
2 CONC band, HELGA Anundsdotter [Balk av Strand], daughter of ANUND Röriksson [Balk av Strand] & his wife Cecilia Magnusdotter.  She married secondly (before 1379) Ya Königsmarck, Vogt of Stockholm Castle.  Valdemar & his wife had one ch
2 CONC ild: 
2 CONT >>>>>>>>>>* (a)       ERIK Valdemarsson (-[1388/96]).  m ERMEGARD --- (-[1402/03].
2 CONT >>>>* e)         RIKISSA Valdemarsdotter (-[1 Sep 1288/19 Apr 1293]).  The Annales Polonorum record the marriage "1285 in octavis sancti Francisci" of "filiam regis Swecie nomine Rithcam" and "dux Primislius maioris Polonie"[195].
2 CONC   m (1285) as his second wife, PRZEMYSŁ Prince of Greater Poland, son of PRZEMYSŁ I Prince of Poznan, Kalisch and Gniezien [Piast] & his wife Elisabeth von Schlesien [Piast] (14 Oct 1257-murdered Rogoźno 8 Feb 1296, bur Posen Cath
2 CONC edral).  He succeeded in 1295 as PRZEMYSŁ II King of Poland. 
2 CONT >>>>* f)          MARIANNA Valdemarsdotter .  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.   1299.  m (Nyköping 1285) as his second wife, RUDOLF von Diepholz, son of --- (-1303 or after
2 CONC ).
2 CONT >>>>* g)         MARGARETA Valdemarsdotter .  The primary source which confirms her parentage has not yet been identified.   Nun at Skänninge Convent 1288. 
2 CONT King Valdemar had one possible illegitimate son by Mistress (1):    h)         [ERIK Valdemarsson ([1273]-).  Brenner doubts his existence, saying he is likely confused with King Valdemar's legitimate son Erik[196].] 
2 CONT * 3.         '''MAGNUS Ladulås Birgersson''' ([1240]-Visingsö 18 Dec 1290, bur Stockholm, Riddarholm Church).  The Annales Lubicenses names "Magno duce fratre suo [=Waldemarus rex Sweorum]" when recording that he deposed his broth
2 CONC er in 1275[197].  He succeeded in 1275 as MAGNUS I Ladulås King of Sweden.   
2 CONT * 4.         '''KRISTINA Birgersdotter '''(-after 1285).  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.   m SIGGE Guttormsson, from Ljuna (-bur Alvastra Abbey).
2 CONT * 5.         '''KATARINA''' .  The Cronica Principum Saxonie names "Katerinam, filiam regis Suecie" as wife of "Sifridum comitem"[198].  m (before 17 Oct 1259) SIEGFRIED Graf von Anhalt in Köthen und Dessau, son of HEINRICH I "der
2 CONC  Fette" Graf von Anhalt und Aschersleben & his wife Irmgard von Thüringen (-after 25 Mar 1298, bur Coswig).
2 CONT * 6.         '''ERIK Birgersson''' (-17 Dec 1275).  “B…Dux Sueorum” donated property to Eskilstuna Kloster by charter dated 16 Jul 1266 which names “filiorum nostrorum…W…Regis Sueorum, Magni Ducis…Ericj ac Benedictj Scolaris”[199]
2 CONC .  Duke in southern Sweden 1275. 
2 CONT * 7.       '''  INGEBORG''' (- 30 Jun 1302, bur Mölln).  The Cronica Principum Saxonie refers to the wife of "Iohannem [filium Alberti dux]" as "filiam regis Suecie"[200].  The Annales Lubicenses record the death in 1302 of "Ingeb
2 CONC urgis, mater Alberti, Iohannis et Erici ducum Saxoniæ, filia Regis Sweonum"[201].  m ([1270]) JOHANN I Herzog von Sachsen, son of ALBRECHT I Herzog zu Sachsen, Engern und Westfalen [Askanier] & his third wife Helene von Braunschwe
2 CONC ig (-30 Jul 1286).
2 CONT * 8.         '''BENGT Birgersson''' ([1254]-25 May 1291).  “B…Dux Sueorum” donated property to Eskilstuna Kloster by charter dated 16 Jul 1266 which names “filiorum nostrorum…W…Regis Sueorum, Magni Ducis…Ericj ac Benedictj Scolari
2 CONC s”[202].  Duke in Finland 1284.  Bishop of Linköping 1286.  Birger Magnusson had one illegitimate son by Mistress (1): 9.          GREGERS Birgersson or Frilloson [Folkingaättens oäkta gren] (-1276, bur Uppsala).  At Ängsjö.  The 
2 CONC Icelandic Annals record the death in 1276 of "Gregorius filius notus Birgeri comitis"[203].  He was ancestor of the Folkingaättens Oäkta Gren family. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' Product MedLands,, Chapter 3. KINGS of SWEDEN 1250-1412 (FOLKINGAÄTTEN) - http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SWEDEN.htm#BirgerMagnussondied1266B
2 CONT
