2 TITL Isabella of Aragon
2 NOTE Isabella of Aragon (1247 – 28 January 1271), infanta of Aragon, was, by marriage, Queen consort of France in the Middle Ages from 1270 to 1277 
3 CONT
3 CONT She was the daughter of King James I of Aragon and his second wife Violant of Hungary, daughter of Andrew II of Hungary.
3 CONT In Clermont on 28 May 1262, she married the future Philip III of France, son of king Louis IX and Marguerite of Provence.
3 CONT
3 CONT Read more about Isabella in her profile.
