1 NOTE EARLDOM of CAITHNESS (XI) 1280?
2 CONT
2 CONT NORSE PREDECESSORS of the EARLS of ORKNEY - subject to King of Norwayuntil after 1379
2 CONT
2 CONT John II, Jarl of Orkney and Earl of Caithness 1284 to a. 1312, b. circa1259. He was one of the signatories of the Scottish letter of 12 Mar.1289/90 to King Edward I about the marriage of his son Edward andMargaret the Maiden, Quee
2 CONC n of Scots. On 13 May 1291 he had a safe conductvalid until 24 June to come to King Edward I, who was then at Norham. Hrwas sum. to the first Parliament of King John Balliol at Scone (10 Feb.1293); had letters of protection dated 
2 CONC 28 Aug. 1296 from King Edward Ivalid for one year from 29 Sep. of that year, and swore fealty to him atMurkle in Caithness Aug. 1297. The name of his wife is not recorded (b).He d. presumably before 1311 and certainly before 28 Oc
2 CONC t. 1312 (c). Hewas suc, by his son. [Complete Peerage, X:Appendix A:30]
2 CONT
2 CONT (b) Saint Clair, gives as his wife "dau. of Graham of Lovat." She musthave d. a. 1299, as, according to the Icelandic Annals (Anderson, 0.3.,Intro., p. Ii), Jarl John in 1299, being then 40, was betrothed toIngibiorg, the two-year
2 CONC -old dau. of Eric II, King of Norway (1280 to1299), by Isabella, sister of King Robert I Bruce.
2 CONT
2 CONT (c) Ingibiorg was betrothed anew in 1311, and On 29 Sep. 1312 was m. toWaldemar, Duke of Finland (d. 1318), and had issue.
