1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Blathach / Bláthóc / Bethóc becomes Bjaðǫk only once brought to Norway as the potential new King Eysteinn's mother.'''  The story is that his father was Harald (originally named Gilla Crist) - also born and bred
2 CONC  in Ireland/Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Claims that she is connected to Gilla Adamnáin as his daughter and Somairle mac Gilla Brigte, King of the Isles (d 1164) (who himself had a daughter named Bethóc) as his Aunt, are as modern as the late 18th Century''' - so, sho
2 CONC rt of decent primary sources, although the naming is similar.
2 CONT
