1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://family.grillenborg.se/sites/all/tng/getperson.php?personID=I15262&tree=tree1
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Toralde Toraldesson, på Berg''' was born circa 1245 in Buskerud, Norway. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Toralde married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34726719921 Ingeborg Gunnarsdatter]. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * 1289 [https://www.geni.com/profile-77000726 Salomon Toraldesson, Biskop i Oslo];
2 CONT * 1295 [https://www.geni.com/profile-17090290 Gunnar I Toraldesson Kane]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died circa 1290 in Berg, Tønsberg, Vestfold, Norway. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ---- Far til den første Gunnar Kane. Opphavet til Kaneætta er noe usikkert, se mer informasjon hos etterkommere. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------
2 CONT -------------------- http://family.grillenborg.se/sites/all/tng/getperson.php?personID=I15262&tree=tree1
2 CONT
2 CONT After reading the debate thread at the National Archives about the Kane family from 2007, I think we need to clean up the tree. There are many uncertainties regarding this family, but what we can be sure of is Nicolaus (Nils) Gunn
2 CONC arsson Kane and Toralde Gunnarsson Kane, III and their father was Gunnar Toraldesson Kane II
2 CONT
2 CONT In post 21 in the debate I linked over, Vigerust answers whether there is any team in a lineage similar to the one we have on Genius (Sigurd Gunnarson ca. 1340 - 1403 Gunnar Toraldeson approx. 1320 - 1414 Toralde 1 Gunnarson ca. 1
2 CONC 300 - 1388 Gunnar Toraldeso ca. 1260 - 1343 Toralde Toraldeson approx. 1220 - 1260 Toralde Kane Brandenburg approx. 1200)
2 CONT
2 CONT "The names Kurt Østbye refers to are unknown to me. But Gunnar Toraldesson Kanes (known 1398-1414) father (Toralde Gunnarsson, known 1366-69) and * possible * grandfather (Gunnar Toraldesson Hvit) both lived in Norway. Gunnar and 
2 CONC Toralde are of Norwegian origin, there is no reason to look for German origin for this family. That the genus Kanitz led the same weapon, as is claimed, is nevertheless something one should draw with in the further research. "
2 CONT
2 CONT I would also recommend everyone to read throughout the debate. That "our man" Toralde Butter hat belongs to Kane's family devastated otherwise. But considering how much uncertainty it is about this family, and basically there are 
2 CONC only hypotheses about Gunnar Kane's father and grandfather: Are there any sources that support this profile: https://www.geni.com/people/Torald- 1-Toraldsson-Kane-på-Berg / 600000 ... It is Gunnar Kane's great-grandfather, but I s
2 CONC uggest that we remove the parents from that profile and rename it to Torald NN Kane, since it is so uncertain.
