1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Harald Ernilsson (Gren)==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Ernils Kettilbjörnsson (Gren)
2 CONT * Gren is a medieval savior family from Östergötland . The family's name survives in the farm name Grensholm . The family died out on the sword side in 1520.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children==
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Torkel Haraldsson (Gren);''' 
2 CONT * '''Sten Haraldsson (Gren);''' 
2 CONT * '''NN Haraldsdotter (Gren)'''
2 CONT * '''Sigrid Haraldsdotter (Gren)''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT == Swedish Diplomatarium's National Archives of Medieval Letters==
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No:[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Harald+Ernilsson+&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=9&postid=sdhk_7556&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 7556]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1359 May 17, of Issue: Skanninge'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Holmger Torkelsson sells to the knight Magnus Nilsson all his estates in Västerlösa in Rogslösa parish (Dals district) for 200 marks Swedish money according to the country's law.
2 CONT The issuer and Mr. Magnus, Bengt Filipsson and Magnus Torkelsson, knights, and Mr. Harald, parish priest in Skänninge, Sjunne Klemensson, councilor in Skänninge, '''Harald Ernilsson''' and Karl Tuveson seal. - https://sok.riksarki
2 CONC vet.se/dokument/sdhk/7556.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Harald+Ernilsson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=5&postid=sdhk_7341&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 7341]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1358 April 11, of issue: Västervik (Gamleby)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Nils Turesson , knight and slayer in Sweden, lends on behalf of King Erik to Harald Ernilsson for faithful service the farm in Hovstad (in Kättilstads parish) owned by Hemming Räv. The issuer seals: SEAL: The seal drawing shows on
2 CONC ly one strip cut from the letter.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK No:[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Harald+Ernilsson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=2&postid=sdhk_4877&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 4877]
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''Dating: 1343 May 25'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Harald Ernilsson sells to Linköping's cathedral 1/8 octagon in Ånväga (Skeda parish, Hanekinds herald), which has previously been pledged to the said cathedral, for 20 land money and gives a fixed amount. - https://sok.riksarkivet
2 CONC .se/dokument/sdhk/4877.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Harald+Ernilsson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_7821&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 7821]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1360 August 7'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Harald Ernilsson announces that to honest man Staffan Nilsson (Stangenberg) he has given 3/4 oak in two bolts in Staby (in Rystad's parish) and ½ ounce of Sigsten Gamle's bol in Mörtlösa Loth (in S: t Lars parish) for 50 marks mon
2 CONC ey.
2 CONT
2 CONT The issuer and brother Johan Ernilsson, the city of Linköping, Birger Karlsson and the citizen Lemeke in Linköping seal.  - https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000007328882131&photo_id=600000013996991482
2 CONC 1&position=0
2 CONT
2 CONT SEAL
2 CONT no. 1, dropped from the seal strip and the bag of non-dyed linen quarantined at the strip; No. 2 of unpainted wax, in bag of unpainted linen (7-star in shield, see J. Raneke, Swedish Medieval Weapons II, 1982, p. 536): S '[..] rge
2 CONC ri. Karlson; Nos. 3 and 4 are missing; no. 5 from the seal strip and the bag of non-dyed linen, which is located at the strip.
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Harald+Ernilsson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=7&postid=sdhk_6942&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 6942]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1356 without a day, of issue: Cut Lunda''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Johan Petersson , subordinate chief in Kinda here on behalf of Mr Bengt Filipsson, certifies that Harald Ernilsson received half Bockstorp (in Oppeby parish) by Anders Clockers against 2 monkeys in Hag (in V. Eneby parish). 12 fas
2 CONC tes are listed. The issuer seals: Seal drawing: on a strip cut from the letter (three beams arranged lilies in shield): Ioannis. Petri - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/6942.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT == SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=Harald+Ernilsson&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=11&postid=sdhk_7416&tab=post&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C#tab 7416]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1358 August, of Issue: Stockholm'''
2 CONT
2 CONT King Erik gives the well-to-do man Harald Ernilsson for his faithful service to the king and the crown 4 attungs - as if on an elm - in Hovstad in Kättilstad parish, who have returned to the crown due to the crimes of Johan Galts,
2 CONC  Hemming Rävs and Ingolf. For ten years, they had not paid taxes or anything else that adds to the crown or done rust service. The issuer seals. - https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/7416.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT == [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Mobil/Artikel/13177 History of the Branch, Family]
2 CONT
2 CONT Branch, medieval Savior, whose family name can be dated to the earliest in 1424. Its oldest known ancestor, Kettilbjörn Knutsson (lived in 1323), was, according to several letters, a brother or, though less likely, a half-brother 
2 CONC to the link-opening rabbi Björn (d. 1329 or 1330), of the years 1312-19. The former son Inge Kettilbjörnsson (still alive in 1335) became a knight shortly before his death. '''His brother Ernils Kettilbjörnsson (still alive in 133
2 CONC 0), known as one of those who in 1320 negotiated with King Magnus Eriksson's guardian government with King Birger's supporters at Viborg, became the father of Harald Ernilsson (still alive in 1360). He probably married a daughter 
2 CONC from the Birger Earl, who is descended from the Birger Earl to the Swedish National Council Torkel Andersson (boat).'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Their son Torkel Haraldsson (d 1402) must in the 1370s for a drop make pilgrimages to Rome, Aachen and Nidaros, among others. Later, he was county governor in several herds in Södermanland and Östergötland. Torkel Haraldsson was d
2 CONC ubbed knight in the fall of 1389, probably at the men's day in Söderköping, where Queen Margareta took over power in Sweden, and was later named as the chief white man at Ämnisholm in Småland. In 1398 he was a member of King Erik'
2 CONC s Union Council, but he never belonged to the Swedish Council.
2 CONT
2 CONT His brother, the governor of the Austrians (South) Sten Haraldsson (still living in 1417) at Ål (now Grensholmen) in Vånga (Ög), became married to a daughter of King Erik Magnusson's counsel Nils Magnusson (Ivar Nilsson's ancestry
2 CONC ) father of the Council of Magnus G (G 1). Her son, the Swedish National Council Ivar G (G 2), became the father of the Swedish National Council Måns G (G 3). The G family extended with two of the latter's sisters, who were still 
2 CONC alive at the beginning of the 1540s. Among its descendants on the women's side was King Gustav I, whose maternal grandmother was brother to G 1. The family name survives in the farm name Grensholmen. It was called G1's seat farm Å
2 CONC l from about 1510 by his son-in-law Erik Ryning, who then owned it.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Links==
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://sv.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gren_(adlig_%C3%A4tt)
2 CONT * http://www.roskildehistorie.dk/stamtavler/adel/svenske/Gren/Gren.htm
2 CONT * http://www.k-h-andresen.dk/slaegt/slaegt_niveau2/slaegt_niveau3/slaegt_niveau4/slaegt_niveau5/slaegt_niveau6/slaegt_niveau7/slaegt_niveau8/slaegt_niveau9/slaegt_niveau10/henrik262144_43981_43984.html
2 CONT * https://sv.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Svenska_sigiller_fr%C3%A5n_medeltiden
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Medieval transcriptions:  A 9, fol. 66r, RA 0201
2 CONT * Post-medieval transcriptions:  Örnhielm: III, p. 813
2 CONT * Nygren, LBH 3, p. 221
2 CONT * Post-medieval transcripts:  Brocman: II Misc. 19:61
2 CONT * DS No. 6034 (for identification of Hemming Fox)
2 CONT * Post-medieval transcripts:  B 16, fol. 131, RA 0202
2 CONT * The brothers Holmger and Magnus Torkelsson and their brothers-in-law Harald Ernilsson and Karl Tuveson also appear in letters 1359 30/7 (SDHK no. 7574 ); cf., however, ÄSF I, p. 57, where 'Tuveson' is assumed to be a misspelling
2 CONC . The identification of the knight Magnus, whose patronymic icon has been omitted in ms (see note in the text apparatus), is made more difficult by the fact that several contemporary knights bore the name Magnus. Possibly refers t
2 CONC o Magnus Knutsson who was then Östgötalagman (ÄSF I, p. 12). He appears as a sailor together with pastor Harald in another land transfer in Skänninge (letter 1358 29/7, SDHK no. 7413 ).
2 CONT * Post-medieval transcripts:  Lars Eriksson Sparre's copybook, hs B 15, fol. 298r, RA 0202
2 CONT * Alla vägar bär till Rom: 75 generationer från von Wachenfeldt och Uggla till, By Bjarne Persson - https://books.google.com/books?id=IqoyDwAAQBAJ&pg=PA94&lpg=PA94&dq=Harald+Ernilsson+(Gren)+%26+Torkelsdotter&source=bl&ots=FDcOrtJ
2 CONC LCL&sig=ACfU3U1W3Y86cN7SulMNjid_50zEy2HYvA&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwi84d_5oOnqAhW2FzQIHXYAC58Q6AEwCHoECAoQAQ#v=onepage&q=Harald%20Ernilsson%20(Gren)%20%26%20Torkelsdotter&f=false
2 CONT * Documents concerning the history of Scandinavia. Chronological register ..., Volume 4, Royal Society for the publication of manuscripts concerning the history of Scandinavia - https://books.google.com/books?id=oTYOAAAAQAAJ&dq=ce
2 CONC cilia%20haraldsdotter%20gren&as_brr=3&hl=sv&pg=PA377#v=onepage&q=cicilia&f=false
