2 CONC ason at a parliament in Scone in Aug 1320 and sentenced to life imprisonment[733].  m secondly ([1323]) as her first husband, JOAN Menteith, daughter of Sir JOHN Menteith of Rusky & his wife --- (-after 20 Mar 1367).  She married 
2 CONC secondly John Campbell Earl of Atholl, thirdly Maurice Moray Earl of Strathearn, and fourthly (before 9 Nov 1347) as his second wife, William Sutherland 5th Earl of Sutherland.  Earl Malise & his first wife had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          MALISE (-killed in battle Neville´s Cross 17 Oct 1346).  He succeeded his father as Earl of Strathearn.  He succeeded his cousin Magnus as Earl of Caithness and Orkney in [1323/29].  He resigned the earldom of Strathea
2 CONC rn [24 Sep/16 Dec] 1332 into the hands of Edward Balliol, was tried for treason in 1344 for so doing, but found innocent[734].  John of Fordun´s Scotichronicon (Continuator) records that "Johannes Ranulphi comes Moraviæ ac etiam c
2 CONC omes de Strathern constabularius Scotiæ…David filius et heres David de Lindsay…Willelmus Fraser…" were killed at Durham 17 Oct 1346[735].  [736]'''m firstly MARY, daughter of ---.'''  '''m secondly ([1325/28]) MATILDA [Marjory] of
2 CONC  Ross''', daughter of HUGH Earl of Ross & his first wife Matilda Bruce (-after 1350).  Earl Malise & his '''first wife''' had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT (a)       MATILDA .  m --- de la Arde . 
2 CONT
2 CONT (b)       EUPHEME . 
2 CONT
2 CONT (c)       AGNES (-before 1360).  m ERNGILS, son of ---.  He was granted the title of Earl of Orkney by the king of Norway in right of his wife but forfeited it in 1375[737]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (d)       ISABEL .  m Sir WILLIAM St Clair, son of ---.  Lord St Clair. 
