1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Henry Sinclair, 2nd Earl of Orkney (c. 1375 – 1422) was a Norwegian nobleman and Pantler of Scotland.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was son of Henry Sinclair, 1st Earl of Orkney by his wife Jean, daughter of John Halyburton of Dirleton. Sinclair was one of those captured following the Battle of Homildon Hill, but released on ransom. He had succeeded his fat
2 CONC her by 1404, and was one of those who accompanied James Duke of Rothesay on his journey to France aboard the Maryenknyght, which was captured by English pirates off Flamborough Head. He followed the prince into captivity, but was 
2 CONC soon released.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Sinclair died of influenza c. 1420.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT In about 1407 he married Egidia Douglas, daughter of Sir William Douglas of Nithsdale and maternal granddaughter of King Robert II of Scotland.
2 CONT * William Sinclair, 3rd Earl of Orkney
2 CONT * Beatrix Sinclair, who married James Douglas, 7th Earl of Douglas.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_II_Sinclair,_Earl_of_Orkney
2 CONT
2 CONT __________________________
