2 CONT Succeeded 1400, died 1420 Married Egida, daughter of Sir William Douglas, thus acquiring the lordships of Nithsdale, the wardenship of the three marches, and six further baronies.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was guardian to James I of Scotland during his minority.  In 1406 the 12-year-old Prince was sent to the French court for education and safety and was accompanied by Sir Henry.  Captured by the English off Flamborough Head, bot
2 CONC h were taken to the Tower of London.  The heir to the Scottish throne remained in captivity for eighteen years, returning home to Scotland in 1424 and then only in exchange for £40,000, a sum described as a bill for the upkeep and
2 CONC  education of the young prince.  Sir Henry obtained his own freedom in 1407 by payment of a ransom.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
