1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The parentage of the Tollak Grøsfjell that is mentioned in 1567 is not known for sure. Some contributors here at Geni, and elsewhere claim that he is ''identical to'' Tollak Assersen Grøsfjell. This seems highly un
2 CONC likely, and may be based on a misreading of secondary sources. The main authority on Heskestad/Helleland, Petrus Valand, [https://www.nb.no/items/5f0e4a8385ea53c3e2060bf36a7ced11?page=66 speculated in 1960] that the 'Tollak Grøsfj
2 CONC ell', mentioned in 1567, may have been a son of Torkel Tollaksen Heltand, mentioned in 1563, who himself was a son of Tollak Assersen Grøsfjell, mentioned in 1521, and his first unknown wife, who held allodial rights at Skadberg f
2 CONC arm. Just three years later, [https://www.nb.no/items/49a8feacccdac4dbc4e1052c4bd159d3?page=45 in 1963], the same Petrus Valand, speculated that the 'Tollak (Tollaksen?) Grøsfjell', mentioned in 1567, may have been a ''son of'' To
2 CONC llak Assersen Grøsfjell. Eight years thereafter, in [https://www.nb.no/items/7030d184bbc50ed3e1dac0748f60b679?page=211 "Heskestad sokn: Gard, ætt og folk"], Petrus Valand stated that the Tollak Grøsfjell that is mentioned in 1567 
2 CONC was most likely a ''grandson of'' Tollak Assersen Grøsfjell. In neither of these cases does Peder Valand suggest that the 'Tollak Grøsfjell' that is mentioned in 1567 was ''identical to'' Tollak Assersen Grøsfjell. The latter theo
2 CONC ry seems to be the most plausible one, but as only one son of Tollak Assersen Grøsfjell is known, it seems most likely (but in no way proved) that the patronym of the Tollak Grøsfjell that is mentioned in 1567 was "Torkelsen".
2 CONT ----
2 CONT http://poulkryger.dk/slaegt..html (Lagt til 27.07.2013)
