1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Christina MacTaggart''', Queen of Mann and the Isles. She was the daughter of  Ferquhard MacTaggart (O'Bjolans), 1st Earl of Ross.
2 CONT
2 CONT > "Some time after his return to Lodhus, Olaf decided to marry again in 1218 to ‘Jauon’ (i.e., Joan) a sister of the Queen of Man. Reginald, the Bishop of the Isles, now took action and convening the Synod, demanded that Olaf must
2 CONC  divorce his wife on the ground that she was cousin german to his first wife. Olaf complained that his first marriage was not confirmed: Bishop Reginald was adamant: Joan had to go. In 1222, Olaf married his third wife, Christina 
2 CONC daughter of Farquhar, Earl of Ross."
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources==
