1 OCCU King of Mann and the Isles
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Magnus Olafsson''', King of Mann and the Isles
2 CONT
2 CONT His brother Harald I, was the last recognized Norse King of Mann and ascended the throne after interruption by more distant and rival relatives. Magnus's official title in Latin was Rex Manniae et Insularum or King of Mann and the
2 CONC  Isles. He married [http://www.geni.com/people/DAUGHTER-OF-EOGAN-OF-ARGYLL/6000000006804155423 Mary of Argyll], daughter of [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E%C3%B3ghan_of_Argyll Eóghan of Argyll], the Lord of the Isles. With his dea
2 CONC th in 1265 the Norse Manx Dynasty ended and Scottish rule began. His son Godred VI later attempted restoration but failed.
2 CONT
2 CONT After 1217, Norwegian [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suzerainty suzerainty] of the Isle of Man became a reality and Norway consequently came into collision with the growing power of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Finally, in 1261, [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_III_of_Scotland Alexander III of Scotland] sent envoys to Norway to negotiate for the cession of the isles, but their efforts led to no result. He therefore initiated hosti
2 CONC lities which terminated in tactical victory for the Norwegians, but significant strategic victory for the Scots, at the often-overstated skirmish of the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Largs Battle of Largs] in 1263. The f
2 CONC ailure of the Norwegians to achieve a major and decisive victory at Largs ended their campaign for that year, and the subsequent death of [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haakon_IV_of_Norway Haakon IV] in [http://en.wikipedia.org/wik
2 CONC i/Orkney Orkney] led to the ascension to the throne of his son [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magnus_VI_of_Norway Magnus VI] and the signing of the 1266 [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Perth Treaty of Perth]. The Treaty of 
2 CONC Perth ceded the islands, including Mann, to Scotland in consideration of the sum of 4,000 marks (known as merks in Scotland) and an annuity of 100 marks.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, Scotland's rule over Mann did not become firmly established until 1275, when the Manx under Godred VI suffered defeat in the decisive [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Ronaldsway Battle of Ronaldsway], near [http://
2 CONC en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castletown,_Isle_of_Man Castletown].
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources==
