1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Hjarrande Halvarsson Hvite==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Hallvar Gunnarsson Hvite and Kristin Sigurdsdotter Magnusson Folkunga 
2 CONT * Born possibly in 1150 - Norge 
2 CONT * From Haakon jarls lid, the city is mentioned only once. To Iceland came a wild-backed man Hallvard white with his ship. He was well traveled, had visited all countries between Norway and Gm · daer and also been north of Bjarmela
2 CONC nd. Hallvard came - https://vf.disnorge.no/system/files/DIS-VF/kilder/tonsberg/Helge_Gjessing_-_Tunsbergs_Historie_i_Middelalderen_til_1536_LQ.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT == Spouse  ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married to '''Helga Sigurdsdatter, prinsesse av Norge''' ca 1155.  Helga Sigurdsdatter (Vestfold, c. 1152 - Bergen, 1202), "frilledatter", "Princess of Norway". Mother: Gunnhild Stadheim Giske (Stadheim, 1130 - 1200). Wife of Hj
2 CONC arande Hallvarson Hvite (Vestlandet, 1140 - Lier, 1220-1230), a nobleman from Western Norway living in 1165, adelsmann på Vestlandet, - https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sigurd_II_of_Norway
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children==
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Gunnar Kongsfrende Hjarrandesson,'''ca 1190 
2 CONT * '''Sigurd Kongsfrende Hjarrandesson,'''ca 1190 
2 CONT * '''Gunnulv Hvite,'''ca 1190 
2 CONT
2 CONT Historians have written he was a decended from king harold fairhair & gyda's dotter aalov (unconfirmed)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Notes for Hjarand White:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Hjarande is a nobleman from western Norway who lived in 1165. Histori. Kker Finn A. Wang argues an article by Hjardane White deleted down from Harald Fairhair and Gyda Eriksen's daughter Aalov (Årbot), who was married to Tore Jarl
2 CONC  Teiande, a son of Ragnvald Mørejarl, but then we do not have all the names of the kindred joints between Aalov and Hjarande We are holding ourselves to the branch Harald Fairhair and down to Helge S. Munn. Finn Wang also writes, 
2 CONC "Hjardande was a Birkebeineran chieftain in the Battle of the chin cheek in 1175 and that Hjardane was very high-pitched the fact that in 1183 at the battle the egg eggs were with King Sverre's son Sigurd Lavare, sister son Håkon 
2 CONC Galen, Sverres Half-sister Peter Steyper.
2 CONT
