2 CONT =='''SDHK-nr:''' [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=magnus++&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=9&postid=sdhk_216&tab=post#tab 216]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dating: 1184 without a day''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT King Knut announces that he as alms donated 2 whole bol (mansiunculas) in fishing1 in Älvkarleby to the Cistercian monks in Julita and their descendants. The witnesses were Archbishop Stefan in Uppsala, Bishop Vilhelm in Strängnäs
2 CONC , Duke Birger, his brothers Magnus and Karl, Finvid Stryker, Sven "owin", "Syctrig brown" and several other great men in the country, clerks and laymen. - https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000006283701220?album_type=photos_of_me
2 CONC &photo_id=6000000138144517866
2 CONT
2 CONT =='''SDHK-nr:''' [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=magnus++&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=11&postid=sdhk_268&tab=post#tab 268]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Swedish Diplomatarium's main directory of medieval letters
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dating 1192 without a day''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT King Knut Eriksson to gentlemen and great men with confirmation of their sale of a third in the fishing lake Sken for three land gold to Nydala monastery. The purchase is confirmed by Bishop Kol, Earl Birger, King's brother Filip,
2 CONC  Earl's brothers Magnus and Karl, Finvid Stryk, the monks Peter Albus and Peter from Norway, the custodian Torald and Styrger's son Tove and the play brothers Hagbard, Gjord and Åke. - https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000006283
2 CONC 701220?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000138144942831
2 CONT
2 CONT =='''SDHK-nr:''' [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=magnus++&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=12&postid=sdhk_287&tab=post#tab 287]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dating 1200 without a day''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT King Sverker Karlsson to the 'princes and the great men' with confirmation of the sale of a third in the fishing lake Sken for three land gold to Nydala monastery and its legal possession thereof. The purchase is confirmed by Bish
2 CONC op Kol, Earl Birger, King Knut's brother Philip, the Earl's brothers Magnus and Karl, Finvid Stryk, the monks Peter Albus and Peter from Norway, the custodian Torald and Styrger's son Tove and the play brothers Hagbard, Gjord and 
2 CONC Åke. Whoever puts obstacles in the way of this is threatened with banishment, and the king urges his successors not to decrease but to increase the support of God's servants.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' Medieval transcripts:  Vid. Perg. 13720509 - Contents Off. 12210000 (DS 833) and 12220000 (DS 834), Shoester Monastery, RA 0107.14. Post-medieval transcripts:  Örnhielm: VIII p. 406 (e. Or. And vid.)
2 CONT
