1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ='''Sigge Guttormsson''', till Ljuna=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Guttorm Guttormsson and Eldrid Jonsdatter 
2 CONT * Sigge Guttormsson to Ljuna was a Swedish stormman from Hogstad parish near Mjölby in Östergötland, died 1283 who is considered the grandson of Earl Guttorm . He was married to Birger Jarls daughter Kristina Birgersdotter (died 1
2 CONC 285).
2 CONT * Birth:	after circa 1220 Sverige
2 CONT * Death: 1283
2 CONT *  Buried: Alvastra Monastery
2 CONT * Guttormsson to Ljuna was a Swedish Greatman from Hogstad near Mjölby in Östergötland, Dead 1283 who is considered the grandson of Guttorm Jarl. He was married to Birger Jarl 's daughter Kristina Birger's daughter (d. 1285). 
2 CONT * Seat yard: Ljuna in Hogstad
2 CONT * Sigge Guttormsson was the stormman in Östergötland in the 13th century, living in Hogstad near Mjölby. 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: '''Kristina Birgersdotter,''' in her second marriage. married to Birger Jarl 's daughter Kristina Birgersdotter. The storm in Östergötland in the 13th century. 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Birger Siggesson gumsehuvud; A son is also known through Sigge Guttormsson's will, written 11 June 1283. '''To his son Birger as the "schooling" the value of his own armor, since it was sold by the testament dean Dean Jng (e 
2 CONC / mouth /?). The young son Birger gets his father's armor, because he seems to be dedicated to a worldly career as a knight. 
2 CONT * '''Helena Siggesdotter; '''Their daughter Helena's daughter is to have been married first to the Danish knight Ingemar Nielsen, and Then to Ulf Holmgersson (Ama). A son is also known by Siggy Guttormssons Testament, written 11 J
2 CONC une 1283.
2 CONT * '''Margaret Siggesdotter''' Their daughter Margareta Kristinadotter was married to the lawyer Leonard Ödesson (Örnfot).
2 CONT
2 CONT =The Swedish Diplomatarium's National Archives of Medieval Letters=
2 CONT
