1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Birger Siggesson (Gumsehuvud) =
2 CONT
2 CONT * Parents: Sigge Guttormsson, till Ljuna and Kristina Birgersdotter (Folkungaätten) (folk young dynasty) 
2 CONT * Brother of Helena and Margareta. Mentioned as barely of age in the father's Testament 1283 in Åkerbo HD
2 CONT * Profession: Squire
2 CONT * Born:1274 in Sundby, Södermanland, Sverige Sweden
2 CONT * Death: December 13, 1352 (61-62) in Sverige Sweden
2 CONT * Husband to NN father to Sigge Birgersson. 
2 CONT * The entire epitaph should therefore be read as follows: Hie illustre thori / pair, quod convixit amori/, Siggo, Christina/, condunturque elemosyna/ Illam famosus / genuit dux pregenerosus/ Nomine Birgerus/, comes hunc Gutthormqu
2 CONC e procerus/In Swedish translation: »Here lies a famous married couple, who lived together in love, namely Sigge and Christina, and they are buried here free of charge because of their alms. She gave birth to the famous and high-bo
2 CONC rn earl named Birger, him the noble earl Gutthorm
2 CONT
2 CONT =Notes=
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigge Guttormsson in the Ljuna testament from June 11, 1283 is preserved. In the testament, the son of Birger is mentioned as a barely authoritative person. Text from the testament: "Oh my dear, my dear, I give my furded coat with
2 CONC  a capuchon - for my son Birger, this armor as a whole, as I have had." The young son Birger gets his father's armor, because he seems to be dedicated to a worldly career as a knight. From, Bo Theutenberg - Folkung and Crossbreake
2 CONC r
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * In 1386-1412. Forstena, not unlikely to be married to a woman from the Mecklenburg-Norwegian family Augustine. Possibly hh in Åkerbo hd in Östergötland 1396-1405. Forstena. Besegl. transaction Bjällbo 27/3 1412 (SD 1554).
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Sigge Birgersson Gumsehuvud'' Ansedel Född 1400 i Västra Tunhem Älvsborgs Län. (P). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/ValdSortering=DatumStigande&PageSize=100&Sokord=Birger&EndastDigitaliserat=False&FacettState=UFwRxg%3Ao%7Cundefined%3Ac%7C&FacettLimits=8n42%2FQ%3A0&AvanceradSok=False&page=77&postid=sdhk_1238&tab=pos
2 CONC t#tab '''SDHK No: 1238, Swedish Diplomatarium's Main Directory of Medieval Letters''']
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dating: 1283 June 11'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigge Guttormsson to Ljunato the brothers in Lödöse 1 mark silver, to two hospitals in Östergötland 1 mark silver, to the monastery in Askeby 1 mark silver, to the monastery in Vreta 1 mark silver, to the brothers in Nyköping 1 ma
2 CONC rk silver, further 1 mark silver as a kind of compensation, which he mentioned to his confessor, and finally to the hospital on Öland 1/2 mark silver. To be able to pay the above he pledges his red clothes and 1 eighth in Västra L
2 CONC juna between the two farms and forbids anyone except the monks in Alvastra or his wife to redeem this eight. He also donates to the church in Linköping his yard in Hogstad with all the concessions and buildings1 and releases all h
2 CONC is slaves. To the priest Nils in Högby he donates his black tunic with surkot and hood, to the priest N. his lined coat with hood, to his son Birger as 'school money' the value of his own armor, since it was sold by the will of th
2 CONC e dean Dean Jng (e / mouth /?). In his wife's discretion, his other weapons will be distributed among Folkvid, Beno Byllasson, Hakvin Röde, Nils Krok, Yandus, Torkil, Peter Långe and Toke, besides a horse, his sword and helmet, wh
2 CONC ich he gives to Yandus. To redeem himself from his crusade promise, he deposits two silver girdles and a silver jug, which is found at the goldsmith Tideman in Söderköping. addition Hakvin Röde, Nils Krok, Yandus, Torkil, Peter Lå
2 CONC nge and Toke, besides a horse, his sword and helmet, which he gives to Yandus. To redeem himself from his crusade promise, he deposits two silver girdles and a silver jug, which is found at the goldsmith Tideman in Söderköping. ad
2 CONC dition Hakvin Röde, Nils Krok, Yandus, Torkil, Peter Långe and Toke, besides a horse, his sword and helmet, which he gives to Yandus. To redeem himself from his crusade promise, he deposits two silver girdles and a silver jug, whi
2 CONC ch is found at the goldsmith Tideman in Söderköping. addition
2 CONT he pledges some goods to resolve a number of monetary debts to private individuals and institutions. Witnesses are his wife Kristina, the left-wing canonists Svennung and Birger, master Otto, brother Knut from Söderköping and his 
2 CONC priest Nils, who also sealed together with the issuer and the link opening chapter.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.geni.com/photo/viewalbum_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000008420798730&photo_id=6000000130860687822&position=0 '''SDHK-nr: 6493''']
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Swedish Diplomatarium's main directory of medieval letters'''
2 CONT
2 CONT =Copy of Birger Siggesson (gumsehuvud) Orginal Will, Dating: December 1352=
2 CONT
2 CONT The prebendary of Linköping Birger Siggesson draws up his will. He donates 60 land money to the cathedral in Linköping building, which Ulf Håkansson owes him; to the Archdeacon Magnus ten marvels, etc., to Leco two silver cups and
2 CONC  his better silver belt, to the sacristan Nils a silver cup, to Nils Jonsson a psalterium. Further gifts to Jonarus Esgeri, Conradus, Askeby and Vreta monastery, Nils in Stång, Johannes Puke and others.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the name of the Lord, Amen. In the Incarnation M ° ccclii on St. Lucia will Byrgerus Siggonis, prebendarius church Lyncopensis, be a severe illness, was still healthy and unharmed, and the goods to which God will write and will
2 CONC  in this manner. In the early construction of the church Lyn [c] opensis said read marks sixty pence, in which the owner Vlpho Hakunsson to do so, as in his letters about this fully contained. Also the Great archidyachono ten mard
2 CONC ilinas off with one of Renault and its Sela. (1) Chief Marcho breuiarie will be better and a cup of silver. The lemons two cups of silver and silver belt is better. Ingeualdo the belt, one silver, one mortar and one of furs and sk
2 CONC ins mardilinis sleeves. Sir Nicholas Sacristan a cup of silver. Sir Nicholas Ionsson a lute. The ionarius Esgerus one pair of clothes with its furraturis. Conrad played with the silver cup with one hand and a lantern. Also any cor
2 CONC ali an elder half marcham money. Campanario place only. Church of St. Lawrence place Blodsverging cured only. Campanario place the two coasts. Brothers serving III March pence piece of skin from his brother Ingemari Vrsini. Holy S
2 CONC pirit marks the fourth house money. Church Thyrnauallum III March. I March Askaby confinement. I March vretu confinement. Also Nicholas of Stang, my dear cousin, one bowl and the silver two hooves of vulture wings, while those sum
2 CONC arios his chair and one thakhut. Stephen Stangaberg a better horn, which have wings and a belt. In the lonari Nesbyt single chair covered with a cloth. Lord Charles ...... ST. dhumos a silver spoon. Sir John Puka a spoon and a met
2 CONC to with one of the mortar. Also Steward and my daughter four weights of red cloth, also half a piece of the heart [i] rights, X March pence a bed with all Preparamento, one red, one pot, one pot for Humulo and a basin, also sorcoc
2 CONC ium is bright red, with furraturis the hood. Also servants about my daily fourteen weights white popirst. Also each of the horse, the sword and the cap iron clippeo. Items were older, single pot. Also östan servant when I had my b
2 CONC oots and spurs. Also Harald Scrømpt a sword with a steel cap. Also, my maid Gyertrudi my white tunic. Also Sigrid my niece a front axle and a culcedram. Also linked to Margaret Neighbor mine, one cow. Then Nicholas pellipario wear
2 CONC  my blauio. Items Bagga Sudurcopie my shoes mixed color with a hood. Also Peter Vglo skin vaccines. Exequtores of this sort of testament I make honorable and that the men of the masters of the Marchis, Leçon the canons, if Ingeual
2 CONC dum prebendary and Nicholas de Stang above-mentioned stages, of which the seals together with the seal of my present need to communiri, feet, and besought, and binding it with the said exequtores, so that through me, and it was or
2 CONC dained effectively more perfect: such and which are less properly and to do in comparison with Suppleant as they should answer before God.
2 CONT
2 CONT Extratext
2 CONT On baksidan Testament of Birgeri Siggonis prebendar.
2 CONT
2 CONT SIOILL n. Intsusa 1-4, 1-2 af sigillremsorna kvar; n. 5 (ett `B '): s' Birgeri. . . gonis.
2 CONT
