2 CONC  from the public-domain Catholic Encyclopedia of 1913.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Saint Elizabeth of Portugal[2] also known as Elizabeth of Aragon (1271 – 4 July 1336) (Elisabet in Catalan, Isabel in both Portuguese and Spanish) was queen consort of Portugal and is a saint of the Roman Catholic Church.
