2 CONT [edit] Marriage and children
2 CONT
2 CONT On 28 May 1262, Philip married Isabella of Aragon, daughter of James I of Aragon and his second wife Yolande of Hungary, daughter of Andrew II of Hungary, and had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. Louis (1265 – May 1276). He was poisoned, possibly by orders of his stepmother.
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. Philip IV (1268 – November 29, 1314), successor as king.
2 CONT
2 CONT    3. Robert (1269 - 1271).
2 CONT
2 CONT    4. Charles (March 12, 1270 – December 16, 1325), Count of Valois.
2 CONT
2 CONT    5. Stillborn son (1271).
2 CONT
2 CONT After Isabella's death, he married on 21 August 1274, Marie de Brabant, daughter of Henry III of Brabant and Adelaide of Burgundy. Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. Louis (May 1276 – May 19, 1319), Count of Évreux.
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. Blanca (1278 – March 19, 1305, Vienna), married Rudolf III of Austria on May 25, 1300.
2 CONT
2 CONT    3. Marguerite (1282 – February 14, 1317), married Edward I of England
