2 CONT ==========================
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret, Princess of Scotland (1260/61–1283), who married Eirik II of Norway 
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander, Prince of Scotland (21 January 1263 Jedburgh – 28 January 1283 Lindores Abbey); buried in Dunfermline Abbey 
2 CONT
2 CONT David of Scotland (20 March 1272 – June 1281 Stirling Castle); buried in Dunfermline Abbey 
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Death of courtier
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret of England (29 September 1240 – 26 February 1275) was a medieval English princess who became Queen of Scots. A daughter of the Plantagenet king Henry III of England and his queen, Eleanor of Provence, she was Queen consor
2 CONC t to Alexander III "the Glorious", King of the Scots.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the second child of Henry III of England and his wife, Eleanor of Provence, and was born at Windsor Castle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret was married on 26 December 1251, at York Minster, to King Alexander III of Scotland, with whom she had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret, Princess of Scotland (1260/61–1283), who married Eirik II of Norway 
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander, Prince of Scotland (21 January 1263 Jedburgh – 28 January 1283 Lindores Abbey); buried in Dunfermline Abbey 
2 CONT
2 CONT David of Scotland (20 March 1272 – June 1281 Stirling Castle); buried in Dunfermline Abbey 
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Death of courtier
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
