1 NOTE     From Ancestral File (TM), data as of 2 January 1996.
1 NOTE Robert de Brus, 6th Lord of Annandale and jure uxoris Earl of Carrick[1] (July 1243 - March 1304 [2]), was a feudal lord in both Scotland and England prior to and during the Second Barons' War, Welsh Wars, and First War of Scottis
2 CONC h Independence. He was the son and heir of Robert de Brus, 5th Lord of Annandale and Isobel de Calre, daughter of the Earl of Gloucester and Hertford.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert's birth date is generally accepted (July 1243[3]) but there is a ongoing debate as to whether Robert and / or his son King Robert The Bruce, were born on the family estate at Writtle Essex.[4][5][6][7].
2 CONT
2 CONT Legend tells that the 27 year old Robert de Brus, was a handsome young man participating in the Ninth Crusade. when Adam de Kilconquhar, one of his companion-in-arms, fell in 1270 at Acre, and Robert was obliged to travel to tell 
2 CONC the sad news to Adam's widow Marjorie of Carrick. The story continues that Marjorie was so taken with the messenger that she had him held captive until he agreed to marry her, which he did in 1271[8][9]. However, since the crusade
2 CONC  landed in Acre on May 9th 1271, and only started to engage the Muslims in late June, the story and his participation in the Ninth Crusade are generally discounted[10][11].
2 CONT What is known is that in:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1264 He had to ransom his own father, after his capture, along with Henry III, Richard of Cornwall, and Edward I at the Battle of Lewes, Sussex. 
2 CONT 1271 He married, without Scottish Royal consent, Marjory, countess of Carrick. As a result she temporarily loses her castle and estates, regained on payment of a fine. 
2 CONT 1278 He swears fealty to Edward I, on behalf of Alexander III at Westminster. 
1 NOTE EARL OF CARRICK; HAD ADDITIONAL 5 SONS & 5 DAUGHTERS
1 NOTE Thebotaw (Thebotan) DOLSaS died, in about the year 721. He was married to Ascrida, the granddaughter of Olaus, King of Norway and daughter of Rognvald.
2 CONT Their son was Elstein Glmure "Ouslein the Noisy".
2 CONT His son, Earl Rognvald (Ranald) (Regenvald), oN&SM&R was married to Giselda (Gisla) who was the daughter of King Charles of France.
2 CONT Their son, Eynor (Turfeynor) IV Jarl of Orkney died about the year 942. His wife was Elmar.
2 CONT Their son, Thorfin T T HAUSSAKLIFFER (SCULLCLEAVER) V, died about the year 960. He was married to Gariola (Grelog) (Grariola) who was the daughter of Duncan (Dungal) Earl of Caithness.
2 CONT Their son, Lodver (Hlodver lodovic) VII Earl of Orkney was married to Audna (Auona) who was the daughter of King Kiarval of Ireland.
2 CONT Their son, Sigurt II DAN DIGRE (THE STOUT) LODVINSON, 2Eoo died in 1014. He married Thora who was the daughter of King Hakon "The Good".
2 CONT Their son, Earl Brusee (Brusius), died in 1033. He was married to Ingiobiorge.
2 CONT Their son, Earl Rognvald (Ragenwald) Ragwold) BRUCESSON, died in 1046. He married Ostrida WALFSON of Gothland the daughter of Ragenwald WALFSON, Earl of Gothland.
2 CONT Their son was Earl Robert (Ulf) DE BRUSEE or DE BRUIS. He married Emma, daughter of Lord Allan of Normandy.
2 CONT Their son, Adam (Adelme) BRUCE, died in 1094. He married Emma RAMSAY the daughter of Sir William RAMSAY.
2 CONT Their son, Robert BRUCE (DE BRUS) 1st Lord of Cleveland & Annandale, was born in 1071 and died in 1141. He married Agnes DE PAGANELL who was born in 1076. She was the daughter of Fulke DE PAGANELL.
2 CONT Their son, Robert BRUCE ( LE MESCHIN), 21oA&IoS, was born in 1103 and died in 1171. He married Eupliemia (Euphemia).
2 CONT Their son, William BRUCE (DE BRUS), VoABaG, was born in 1142 and died in 1215. He married Christina.
2 CONT Their son, Robert DE BRUS (THE NOBLE), 4th Lord of Annamdale, was born in 1183 and died in 1245. He married Isabel (Isabelle) who was born in 1226 and died in 1251. She was the daughter of David Earl of Huntingdon & Garrioch.
2 CONT Their son, Lord Robert BRUCE, 5th of Annandale & Cleveland, was born in 1210 an died 31 Mar 1295. He married Isabel DE CLARE who was born on 2 Nov 1236 and died in 1295.
2 CONT Their son, Robert BRUCE (DE BRUS), 1st Earl of Carrick & VIth of Annandale, was born in Jul 1243 and died in 1304. He married Countess Marjorie (Margaret) of Carrick who died in 1292.
2 CONT Their son, Sir Thomas BRUCE was born in 1307. He married Mary ERSKINE who was the daughter of Sir John ERSKINE of Erskine.
2 CONT Their son, Sir Thomas BRUCE (BRUS), died in 1330.
2 CONT His son, Sir Thomas BRUCE (DE BRUYS) died in 1358 or 59. He married Marjorie CHARTERIS of Stenhouse.
2 CONT Their son, Sir Robert (Roberto) BRUCE (DE BRUYS), 1st Baron of Clackmannan & Rait, died in 1403. He married Isabel STEWART of Rosyth the daughter of Sir Robert STEWART of Durrisdear & Innermeath.
2 CONT Their son, Edward BRUCE (DE BRUS), of Stanehouse, died in 1417. He married Agnes D'ERTH (AIRTH), the daughter of Sir William AIRTH (D'ERTH).
2 CONT Their son, Sir Robert BRUCE, of Arthe (Airth) died on 6 Jan 1450. He married a LEVINGSTONE, daughter of Sir Alexander LEVINGSTONE of Callender.
2 CONT Their son was Sir Alexander BRUCE (DE BRUS) of Stanhouse & Airth. He married Margaret FORRESTER the daughter of Sir Malcolm FORRESTER of Torwoodhead.
2 CONT Their son, Sir John BRUCE (THE BRUS), of Stanehouse & Airth died in 1483. He married Elizabeth MENTEITH who was the daughter of Sir William MENTEITH of Kerse.
2 CONT Their son, Sir Robert BRUCE, Knight of Stanehouse & Airth died in 1483. He married Euphemia MONTGOMERIE, daughter of Lord Alexander MONTGOMERIE.
2 CONT Their son, Sir Robert BRUCE, died in 1548. He married Janet FORRESTER, the daughter of Sir William FORRESTER of Carden.
2 CONT Their son, Sir Alexander BRUCE, 3rd Baron of Airth, died in 1603. He married Janet LEVINGSTONE daughter of 5th Lord LEVINGSTONE.
2 CONT Their son, Sir William BRUCE, died in 1603. He married Jean (Jane) FLEMING, Lady Airth, the daughter of VIth Lord FLEMING.
2 CONT Their son, Sir William BRUCE, 1st Bt. Stenhouse & Airth, died in 1630.He married Rachael JOHNSTONE, the daughter of Joseph JOHNSTONE of Hiltoun.
2 CONT Their son, Sir William BRUCE 2nd Bt. Stenhouse & Airth was born in 1621. He married Helen DOUGLAS, daughter of Sir William DOUGLAS of Cavers.
2 CONT Their son, Sir William BRUCE, 3rd Bt. Stenhouse & Airth was born in 1661 and died in 1682. He married Margaret ELPHINSTONE the daughter of Robert ELPHINSTONE of Quarole.
2 CONT Their son, Sir William BRUCE, 4rd Bt. Stenhouse & Airth, died in 1721. He married Margaret BOYD, daughter of Sir John BOYD of Trochrg.
2 CONT Their son, Sir Michael BRUCE, 6th Bt. Stenhouse & Airth, died in 1795. He married Mary AGNEW, the daughter of General Sir Andrew AGNEW Bt. of Locknaw.
2 CONT Their son, Sir William BRUCE, 7th Bt. Stenhouse & Airth, died in 1827. He married Mary Ann Cunningham FAIRLIE, the daughter of Sir William Cuningham FAIRLIE of Robertland & Fairlie, Bt.
2 CONT Their son, Captain William Cunningham BRUCE, wa born in 1798 and died in 1842 in Bombay, India. He married Jane Catherine CLARK, the daughter of William CLARK.
2 CONT Their son, Sir William Cunningham BRUCE, 9th Bt. Stenhouse & Airth, was born in 1825 and died in 1906. He married Charlotte Isabella O'GRADY, the daughter of Hon. Waller O'GRADY.
2 CONT Their son, Sir William Waller BRUCE, 10th Bt. Stenhouse & Airth, was born in 1856 and died in 1912. He married Angelica Mary SELBY, the daughter of General George SELBY.
2 CONT Their son, Sir Michael Selby BRUCE, 11th Bt. Stenhouse & Airth, was born in 1894 at Ensenada, Mexico and died on 26 May 1957 at Vancouver, British Colombia, Canada. He married Margaret Helen BINNS, daughter of Sir Arthur Lemmon BI
2 CONC NNS M.C., C.B.E.
