1 NOTE NORSE PREDECESSORS of the EARLS of ORKNEY - subject to King of Norwayuntil after 1379
2 CONT
2 CONT MAGNUS III, Jarl of Orkney and Earl of Caithness 1256 to 1273. He was atBergen when King Hakon IV (1217 to 1263) started in May 1263 on hisexpedition to the Western Isles and was given a good longship; but he wasleft behind in Ork
2 CONC ney when the King started south for the raid in theFirth of Clyde which ended after the engagement at Largs 2 Oct. 1263. TheKing returned to Orkney on 29 Oct., took to his bed and died at Kirkwall,16 Dec. 1263. Jarl Magnus III see
2 CONC ms to have returned to Norway, perhapswith the body of King Hakon IV, as King Magnus VI sent "one of his bestfighting captains, the Baron Ogmund Kraekidanz," to Orkney ‘with power toguard the land" in 1264. Nothing further is reco
2 CONC rded about Jarl MagnusIII Gibbonsson except that he entered into a contract of privileges withKing Magnus VI and the date of his death in 1273. He left two sons,Magnus and John. [Complete Peerage, X:Appendix A:29]
