1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Agrippina Rostislavna''' or '''Agraphena Rostislavna''' (d. December 21, 1237) - the wife of Igor (Ingvar) Glebovich, the prince of Ryazan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Agrippina Rostislavna, known only from the "Tale of the Devastation of Ryazan by Batu", was the mother of Yuri Ingvarevich (or Yuri Igorevich) - prince of Ryazan. Since Yury Igorevich is traditionally considered the prince of Ryaz
2 CONC an during the Mongol invasion, Agrippina Rostislavna is considered the wife of Igor Glebovich, and not Ingvar Igorevich.
2 CONT
2 CONT Presumably, she was the youngest daughter of Rostislav Mstislavich, the prince of Smolensk and Kyiv, who died in 1167 at the age of about 60 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT She died in 1237 together with her son Yuri and his wife during the siege of Ryazan by Batu.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: probably Rostislav Mstislavich - the Great Prince of Kyiv (1159-1167).
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband: Igor (Ingvar) Glebovich (d. in 1194) - Principal Prince of Ryazan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Yuri (killed 1237) - Prince of Ryazan (1217-1235).
2 CONT # Roman (killed in 1237) - Prince of Kolomna.
2 CONT # Oleg (d. 1258) - Grand Duke of Ryazan (1252-1258).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT AGRAFENA Rostislavna (-murdered Dec 1237).  m IGOR Glebovich Prince of Riazan, son of GLEB Rostislavich Prince of Riazan & his wife Iefrosina Rostislavna of Pereyaslavl (-1194). 
2 CONT
2 CONT From source: http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/RUSSIA,%20Rurik.htm#OlegSviatoslavichdied1180
