0 @N6000000002187742682@ NOTE Henry II Sinclair, Earl of Orkney
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Henry II Sinclair, Earl of Orkney (circa 1375 – 1422) was a Scottish nobleman.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was son of Henry Sinclair, 1st Earl of Orkney by his wife Jean, daughter of John Halyburton of Dirleton, and succeeded his father in 1404. In about 1407 he married Egidia Douglas, daughter of William Douglas of Nithsdale and ma
1 CONC ternal granddaughter of King Robert II of Scotland; they were the parents of William Sinclair, 3rd Earl of Orkney, and Beatrix Sinclair, who married James Douglas, 7th Earl of Douglas.
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Henry Sinclair Earl of Orkney
1 CONT 1404–1422 Succeeded by
1 CONT William Sinclair
0 @N6000000003615429683@ NOTE Henry Sinclair, 2nd Earl of Orkney, b. c 1375, d. 1 Feb 1420/1, son of Henry Sinclair, Lord of Roslin, Earl of Orkney, and Jean, daughter of Sir Walter Haliburton of Dirleton.  [Magna Charta Sureties]
1 CONT
1 CONT -------------------------
1 CONT
1 CONT EARLDOM OF ORKNEY [SCT] (II)
1 CONT
1 CONT HENRY (SINCLAIR), EARL OF ORKNEY [SCT], 1st son and heir, succeeded his father. In 1402 he was captured at the battle of Homildon Hill; but he was probably freed before 24 January 1403/4. In March 1405/6 he sailed for France with 
1 CONC Prince James, who had been committed to his care by Robert II; but they were captured at sea on 22 March by men of Yarmouth and Cley (Norfolk), taken to Henry IV and sent to the Tower. He was still a prisoner at the end of 1407. I
1 CONC n 1409 he was engaged in negotiations for the release of James, now King. In 1412 he went to France with the Earl of Douglas [SCT]. He was still living 23 November1419.
1 CONT
1 CONT He married, before 17 November 1407, Jill, daughter and heir of Sir William DOUGLAS, of Nithsdale, by Jill, daughter of ROBERT II, King of Scotland. He died probably 1 February 1420/1, of influenza. His widow married, 2ndly, after
1 CONC  29 April 1422, Alexander STEWART, 3rd son of Murdoch, 2nd Duke of ALBANY [SCT], with whom he was beheaded at Stirling, 25 March 1425. She survived him, and was living in 1438. [Complete Peerage X:95-6, (transcribed by Dave Utzing
1 CONC er)]
