1 CONT
1 CONT On January 6, 1205 he was crowned again with great ceremony by Adolpha t Aix-la-Chapelle, though it was not till 1207 that his entry into Col ogne practically brought the war to a close. A month or two later Phil ip was loosed fro
1 CONC m the papal ban, and in March 1208 it seems probable that a treaty was concluded by which a nephew of the pope was to marr y one of Philip's daughters and to receive the disputed dukedom of Tus cany. Philip was preparing to crush 
1 CONC the last flicker of the rebellion in Brunswick-Lüneburg when he was murdered at Bamberg, on June 21, 120 8, by Otto of Wittelsbach, count palatine in Bavaria, to whom he had r efused the hand of one of his daughters. Philip was a 
1 CONC brave and handso me man, and contemporary writers, among whom was Walther von der Vogel weide, praise his mildness and generosity.
