1 CONC s husband died at Villafranca de Penadres where he was buried. His being gracious had made a good impression in Sicily but he had also been too cautious. Pope Honorious IV now decided it was time to restore peace in Italy, but als
1 CONC o wanted Sicily returned to the House of Anjou as it had been a previous pope who had made Charles of Anjou its king. The Sicilians, however, were distrustful of the generous promises of the pope and preferred their new king, Cons
1 CONC tance's son, Jaime, who would become known as "The Just". Jaime was about nineteen years old, whereas the new king of France, Philippe IV "The Fair", was only seventeen.   In February 1286 Jaime was crowned at Palermo. Discovering
