0 @N6000000000337154846@ NOTE (Research):1272-1337, king of Sicily (1296-1337), 3d son of Peter III (Pedro III) of Arag≡n.When his brother, who was James II, Frederick was his regent in Sicily. In 1295 James renounced Sicily in favor of the Angevin king of Nap
1 CONC les, Charles II, but the Sicilians rebelled and crowned Frederick. A war ensued in which Frederick fought his own brother, now Charles's ally. In the Peace of Caltabellotta (1302) Charles and Pope Boniface VIII recognized Fredrick
1 CONC  as king of Trinacria (an ancient name for Sicily) for his liftime. At his death the kingdom was revert to the Angevin dynasty of Naples.  Although Frederick married a daughter of Charles, war with Naples resumed in 1312. Frederic
1 CONC k, allied successively with Holy Roman Emperors Henry VII and Louis IV, retook the title of king of Sicily and, with his son Peter was crowned in 1322.  The war continued after Frederick's death.
