0 @N6000000005076836444@ NOTE Beatrice of England was born on 25 June 1242 at Bordeaux, Dauphine, France.2 She was the daughter of Henry III, King of England and Eleanor of Provence. She married John II de Montfort de Dreux, 2nd Earl of Richmond, son of Jean I
1 CONC  de Dreux, Duc de Bretagne, on 22 January 1260 at Abbey of St. Denis, Saint-Denis, Île-de-France, France.2 She died on 24 March 1275 at age 32 at London, England.3 She was buried at Grey Friars Church, Greenwich, London, England.3
1 CONT      From 22 January 1260, her married name became de Dreux.
1 CONT Children of Beatrice of England and John II de Montfort de Dreux, 2nd Earl of Richmond
1 CONT Henry de Dreux d. 12841
1 CONT Arthur II de Montfort, Duc de Bretagne+ b. 1262, d. 13121
1 CONT John de Bretagne, 3rd Earl of Richmond b. c 1266, d. 17 Jan 1333/341
1 CONT Marie de Bretagne de Dreux+ b. 12681
1 CONT Pierre de Dreux, Comte de Léon b. c 1269, d. 13121
1 CONT Blanche de Bretagne b. c 1270, d. 13271
1 CONT Alice de Dreux b. 1274, d. c 13291
1 CONT Citations
1 CONT [S106] Royal Genealogies Website (ROYAL92.GED), online ftp://ftp.cac.psu.edu/genealogy/public_html/royal/index.html. Hereinafter cited as Royal Genealogies Website.
1 CONT [S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 73. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
1 CONT [S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family, page 74.
0 @N6000000005076836435@ NOTE Margaret of England, Princess of England was born on 29 September 1240 at Windsor Castle, Windsor, Berkshire, England.2 She was the daughter of Henry III, King of England and Eleanor of Provence. She was also reported to have been
1 CONC  born on 5 October 1240 at Windsor Castle, Windsor, Berkshire, England. She married Alexander III 'the Glorius', King of Scotland, son of Alexander II 'the Peaceful', King of Scotland and Mary de Coucy, on 26 December 1251 at York
1 CONC  Minster, York, Yorkshire, England.1 She died on 26 February 1275 at age 34 at Cupar Castle, Cupar, Fife, Scotland.2 She was buried at Dunfermline Abbey, Dunfermline, Fife, Scotland.2
1 CONT      Margaret of England, Princess of England was also known as Princess Margaret of England.
1 CONT Children of Margaret of England, Princess of England and Alexander III 'the Glorius', King of Scotland
1 CONT Margaret of Scotland, Princess of Scotland+ b. 28 Feb 1261, d. 9 Apr 1283
1 CONT Alexander of Scotland, Prince of Scotland b. 21 Jan 1264, d. 17 Jan 12841
1 CONT David of Scotland, Prince of Scotland b. 20 Mar 1273, d. Jun 12811
