1 CONT In 1306 the son of Robert de Bruce VII, Robert de Bruce VIII (brother to Mary Bruce of Scotland our ancestor) , usually known as Robert Bruce, became king of Scotland as Robert I.  The Scottish throne passed to his son, David Bruc
1 CONC e, known as King David II; he died without an heir. David's nephew, also the grandson of King Robert I, ascended to the Scottish throne as Robert II and founded the Stuart house of kings of England and Scotland.[grosenbaum3.ged]
1 CONT
